sackboy a big adventure has absolutely  blown  me away from the gameplay to the  collectibles to the level design and yes  britney spears  believe it or not that's not the only  bit of licensed music you'll instantly  recognize  in this game seriously it is full of so  many  surprises starting with the fact that  it's legit amazing  so today we're going to review sackboy  of big adventure and share a few more of  the surprises in store for you with this  title  but not too many after all you don't  want to spoil everything let's get into  it  people of the internet retro wrecking  tour here if we're meeting for the first  time i'm just a dad who loves games and  the stories they tell  we post videos every week here on  youtube and also stream over on twitch  when i put zac boy a big adventure on my  2020 christmas list i'll be honest  it was mainly a game i added so i could  have something new for my six-year-old  son and i to play together on our new  ps5  he loved astros playroom which i have a  breakdown up here on my channel  but we wanted something we could enjoy  together well little did i know that  dear old dad here would actually be  gifted one of the  best platformers i've seen in years  seriously guys we're talking nintendo  and  mario level quality here now if you've  played the old little big planet games  you're probably thinking yeah  okay well i played those two and to be  honest while they were cute with lots of  creativity i never found the gameplay to  be all that fun or innovative really the  controls were clunky the gameplay was  decent but when most folks think of  littlebigplanet they likely think of the  many  fan created levels rather than the  actual gameplay itself  that goes completely out the window with  sac boy a big adventure which was  released  alongside the ps5 back in november it's  also available on ps4 however but what's  so great about it for starters this is  not just  another little big planet game with a  new title slapped on this is a 3d  platformer developed by sumo digital and  not  media molecule the original creators of  the series true  i appreciate media molecule and what  they did in terms of customization  co-op and level creation with the  original games but sackboy a big  adventure is the best  game so far in the series and it's so  different right away you'll notice how  well sackboy controls especially  compared to the floatiness of the  original games  here sacboy's movement is responsive and  tight he can run  jump punch grab roll and do this little  extra floaty jump  thing basically it helps him cross  larger gaps the game is divided up into  a series of hub worlds and while it's  described as a 3d platformer there are a  number of different ways sumo switches  up the perspective throughout the game  with tweaks to level design along the  way  it does operate from a fixed perspective  which kind of gives it the feel of  something like super mario 3d world  95 of the time the camera is rock solid  there are a couple of times where the  perspective is a little bit off and it  makes it hard to judge  distance between two platforms for  example but this is incredibly rare  sac boy does a phenomenal job with  pacing steadily introducing new  mechanics as you go and then finding new  ways to alter those mechanics so the  gameplay never grows stale  most of the footage you see here is from  the game's earliest levels but as you  get further into the game you'll find  special mechanics or unique items that  you'll only use during a specific level  or even a specific section of a level  i'm not going to spoil them all here but  i will tease that you'll be doing a lot  more than just running  jumping and punching and not in a  gimmicky way either it completely feels  natural here in sacboy which is made  possible by the game's outstanding level  design you'll find plenty of familiar  platforming mechanics but there are  definitely some unique twists here as  well  each level has a plethora of different  collectibles to find  and challenges to complete there are  also hundreds of different costume  pieces for your sack person some of  which  are found hidden throughout the levels  and others that you can purchase with  gold you collect  in-game you certainly won't be making  your own levels or having the wide range  of customization that we saw in the  littlebigplanet games  but you will have a variety of different  cosmetics to unlock that will  alter the appearance of your sack person  there are different hair styles  helmets glasses shirts pants emotes  facial expressions and even different  fabrics for the sack person underneath  it all sacboy strikes that perfect  balance of presenting just enough of a  challenge to be difficult but not too  frustrating for inexperienced gamers to  lose interest  there are also plenty of ways for  hardcore gamers to challenge themselves  with the game's time  trial levels and many hidden  collectibles although you can play  sackboy solo the game shines brightest  when you play alongside a friend or even  a group of friends as a total of four  players can team up  online play certainly is supported here  but my son and i have had an  absolute blast giving it the old couch  co-op experience  i should also note here that the game  does indeed support cross play between  ps4 and ps5 so if you have friends say  who are on a different system from you  it's nice to know you can still play  together  okay now let's talk about that music i  did not expect  licensed music to be in this game like  at all guys i have no idea maybe they  announced this beforehand maybe this was  a well-known thing but for me it came as  a total surprise when certain hit songs  started playing  out of nowhere i gave you one already  but honestly i don't want to spoil the  rest of them if you really want to know  though i am going to include the  official spotify playlist  in the description below so you can  check that out if you really really  really want to know the songs what's  crazy is it's not just  about the music guys it's not just kind  of playing in the background the level  itself actually reacts to the beat and  there are even moments where it has a  direct  impact on the gameplay for example the  timing of the beat could be the exact  moment you need to jump to another  platform or when you need to be ready  for an enemy to attack  if you can't tell already from the  footage here the graphics and art style  are phenomenal  the game's style in particular helps  feed into the overall charm with lively  worlds filled with obstacles enemies and  interactive objects that are all  pleasing to the eye  keep in mind this is footage all running  on a ps5 at a rock solid 60 fps  for more detailed overview of the game's  performance you should check out digital  foundry's breakdown of the game which  i've also linked  in the description there are boss fights  throughout the game as well which will  usually test your ability to use  recently introduced gameplay mechanics  or special items you've obtained i don't  read as many video game reviews as i  used to and while i had heard a few  rumblings that sackboy was better than  expected i have to say it has completely  exceeded my expectations the main story  can be beaten probably in around 10  hours but if you're looking for all the  collectibles doing the co-op levels  testing your platforming skills with the  time trials you could easily spend 25 to  30 hours here  so is there anyone i wouldn't recommend  sackboy to i think that's a more valid  question guys the only people i could  think of are those who maybe don't enjoy  platformers and prefer to play alone at  all times if you're a fan of platformers  but prefer solo i do think sackboy is  still worth your while  just know that you won't be able to  experience all the game has to offer by  going it  only alone i give sackboy a big  adventure a  big thumbs up and recommend it to anyone  who enjoys platformers or wants  something fun and lighthearted to play  with family and friends  now if any of you out there have kids  little brothers little sisters who  you want to play this game alongside i  cannot recommend it enough it has been  so incredibly fun to play this alongside  my son  we have laughed so many times because  the game just sets itself up so well for  these hilarious moments where  you may fail but you just have to laugh  at yourself because of it and it also  gives you plenty of opportunities to  like help out the other person so  there's a lot of teamwork involved  and then one of my favorite things is at  the end of each level it'll show you who  got the high score for that level and  you're presented with a trophy  but if the other character runs up and  hits you they can actually take the  trophy from you  of course my six-year-old just cackles  maniacally when he does this he loves it  honestly he's played and enjoyed  a lot of games so far the past couple  years especially throughout the pandemic  he really enjoyed animal crossing he  really enjoyed super mario odyssey  i would certainly put this one right up  there with those three that's how much  we've enjoyed it together  if you found this video helpful please  consider giving it a like and if you  want to stick around and be part of the  community here then consider subscribing  to the channel where we post videos  every week  as always thank you all so much for  watching i'll talk to you again soon
 

